===Ascension Form Experience===
Ascension forms have their own experience pool that scales slightly differently than the base classes. They need a slightly lower '''1000''' XP to reach level 2, but this requirement scales a little faster and is multiplied by '''1.2''' for every subsequent level.

XP to reach next level:
<br><math>1.2^{L - 1} \times 1000</math>
<br>Total XP to reach Level '''n''':
<br><math>\left( 1.2^{n-1} - 1 \right) \times 5000</math>
<br>where:
<br><math>L = \text{Current Level}</math>

===Ascension XP Sources===
In addition to having their own experience pool, each Ascension form gains experience differently.

{{ClassTooltip|Tempest}}:

Gains experience for each cast Evocation and over time for each active Incantation and Summoning Spell.

Gain <br><math>0.13 \times \text{H} \times \text{E}</math> XP per second

Gain <br><math>8 \times \text{H} \times \text{IS}</math> XP per second

Where:
<br><math>\text{H} = \text{Ascension form Experience Bonus}</math>
<br><math>\text{E} = \text{Total Evocation casts per second}</math>
<br><math>\text{IS} = \text{Total number of active Incantations and Summons}</math>

Note: For evocations cast, this is based on the real cast rate of the spell and is not affected by multipliers. If your spell, such as {{SpellTooltip|Jas'Aham's Missile Storm}}, has multipliers boosting its displayed cast rate you will need to confirm what it's base maximum cast rate is. By opening your Spellbook and looking in the 3rd tab, you can find your current maximum cast rate for spells. Add to this the bonus cast rate from spell memetics levels on the individual evocations (+1 cast rate per 2 levels) and you will have your base maximum cast rate for the Exp Formula.

{{ClassTooltip|Demiurge}}:

Gains experience over time based on your T2 Character Class's Level. 

Gain <br><math>\frac{ \left( \text{L} - 200 \right)}{10} \times \text{H} \times 4</math> XP per second. 

Where:
<br><math>\text{H} = \text{Ascension form Experience Bonus}</math>

Notes: 
If XP value is below 1, round up to 1. Actually gains exp 4x a second, but for simplicity the formula has been adjusted for XP/sec.

{{ClassTooltip|Dread}}:

Gains experience over time based on both pet's levels.

Gain <br><math>\left( \text{P1} ^{0.5} + \text{P2} ^{0.5} \right) \times \text{H} \times 1.36</math> XP per second

Where:
<br><math>\text{H} = \text{Ascension form Experience Bonus}</math>
<br><math>\text{P1 and P2} = \text{Level of each Pet}</math>

{{ClassTooltip|Defiance}}:

Gains experience over time based on autoclicks performed per second.

Gain <br><math>\text{A} ^{0.5} \times \text{H} \times 3</math> XP per second

Where
<br><math>\text{H} = \text{Ascension form Experience Bonus}</math>
<br><math>\text{A} = \text{Autoclicks performed in the last second}</math>
Note: If XP value is below 1, round up to 1.

==Pet Experience==
[[Pets]], just like your character, can accumulate experience and level up. Unlike your character, however, pets accumulate experience in various different means. Pet experience is unrelated to character experience: earning one doesn't necessarily increase the other. Pets become stronger as they level up, and some even scale from the experience they have.

Pet experience gained can be increased by various [[Upgrades]], as well as by the passive ability and certain spells of the {{ClassTooltip|class_name = Demonologist}} and {{ClassTooltip|class_name = Oni}}.

===Tier 1 Pets===
The experience needed by Tier 1 Pets to reach the next level starts at 100 to reach level 2, and is multiplied by 1.16 every subsequent level.

XP to reach next level:
<br><math>1.16^{L - 1} \times 100</math>
<br>Total XP to reach Level '''n''':
<br><math>\left( 1.16^{n-1} - 1 \right) \times 625</math>
<br>where:
<br><math>L = \text{Current Level}</math>

