==Ability Power==
Each [[Classes|Class]], [[Pet]], and [[Ascension Forms|Ascension Form]] has an Ability unique to them.  These abilities may be seen in the tooltip, by mousing over the portraits.  Each ability typically has multiple sources of scaling, but almost always include their own '''Ability Power'''.
*Character Ability Power is abbreviated as '''CAP'''.
*Pet Ability Power is abbreviated as '''PAP'''.
*Ascension Ability Power is abbreviated as '''AAP'''.

Ability Power can be increased by [[Upgrades]], [[Items]], [[Spells]], [[Gods]], and a few other, lategame, features.

Refer to individual Class, Pet, and Ascension pages to see their abilities and the formulas involved.

==Idle Mode==
[[File:IdleBar back.png|thumb|right]]
[[File:IdleBar Progress.png|thumb|right]]
[[File:IdleBar Full.png|thumb|right]]
'''Idle mode '''is a mechanic in the game that rewards the player for not clicking the orb. Idle mode activates if the orb hasn't been clicked for 30 seconds, found to the left of the Character portrait, indicated with black & orange for Charging, and blue when Activated. Once Idle mode activates, and you get a bonus to your production to Mana.

The Idle mode production bonus can be increased by certain [[upgrades]] and the [[Attributes]] in Patience attribute.

The class ability of the {{ClassTooltip|Necromancer}} also increases your Idle bonus, and he also has access to spells capable of further increasing it. [[Spells]] such as {{SpellTooltip|Nightfall}} & {{SpellTooltip|Synthetic Entity}} can only gain charges while in Online Idle mode.

The {{PetTooltip|Zombie}}'s and the {{PetTooltip|Risen Giant}}'s abilities further increase your income based on your Idle bonus, and their autoclicks can claim your manual click shard pool without the need to leave Idle mode.

Idle mode is a huge boost for spellburst combos, and thus it is highly recommended in almost all cases to activate it before unleashing your spells.

''(You should ALWAYS set off your combos while in '''Idle Mode''' with as much '''[[Void Entities|Void mana]]''' as you can)''

==Void Entities==

'''Void Entities''' are glowing forms of energy that are summoned through the Void Traps within your room. When clicked, they give [[Experience]] and Void Mana, which temporarily gives a large boost to your mana production. The Void Entities can only be contained within the Void Traps for a short amount of time, so you have to be diligent to click them quickly. There are [[Upgrades]] that are used to increase duration in traps, and when combined with {{SpellTooltip|Void Lure}} (or {{SpellTooltip|Void Prison}}), can result in having multiple Void Entities on screen in order to collect more Void Mana, which is very important in making spell combos stronger.

The {{ClassTooltip|Voidmancer}} uses the power of the Void to benefit his spells and power by summoning more strength and utility through having Void Mana. He also has the added ability to become stronger while there are unused Void Entities still in traps.

The {{PetTooltip|Voidfiend}} gains experience through collecting Void Entities. It also creates Void Mana every 10 seconds.

Spells can also collect and create Void Mana:
* {{SpellTooltip|Void Radiance}}, which works by generating mana based on Void Entities left within the Void Traps.
* {{SpellTooltip|Synthetic Entity}} creates a Void Entity within an open Void Trap after 10 minutes of charging.
* {{SpellTooltip|Void Syphon}} (Voidmancer) creates multiple Void Entities which are automatically collected ''(they also give experience)''.

Void Entities are also boosted through '''Insight''' [[Attributes|Attribute]] points.

Info upon Void Entities can be found by '''Hovering''' over the Void Mana next to the Hero and within the '''More Statistics''' ''("S")'' page, providing: Current void mana, Void mana per entity, Entities spawn rate (%), Entities life time, Increase profit by point (%), and Degeneration rate.

There are also [[Achievements]] ("A") that can be earned through collecting Void Mana and Void Entities.

===Spawn Rate===
Void Entities have an ''average'' base spawn time of 300 seconds. The range at which they can spawn is between .65 - 1.35 (a range of .35); thus Void Entities can spawn anywhere from 195 ~ 405 seconds.

The rate at which Void Entities spawn can be altered through some [[Upgrades]] and through using the spells {{SpellTooltip|Void Lure}} & {{SpellTooltip|Void Prison}}.

===Degeneration Rate===
Every second, Void Mana decreases by '''1%''' of its current value, and by 2'''.5'''.

Both of these values are affected by the Degeneration rate found in the Statistics. For example, a {{ClassTooltip|Voidmancer}} with the [[Upgrades#Voidmancer|Void Stability Upgrade]] (total 32.5% Degeneration rate) will lose 0.325% of his current Void Mana and a further 1.1375 every second.

